<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Keeps the media-control icons alive through resource shrinking.

  audio_service names its notification icons as strings from Dart —
  'drawable/audio_service_play_arrow', '…_pause', '…_stop' — and resolves them
  at runtime with Resources.getIdentifier. A reference expressed as a string is
  invisible to the shrinker, so a release build drops them, getIdentifier
  returns 0, and building the media session throws:

      java.lang.IllegalArgumentException:
      You must specify an icon resource id to build a CustomAction

  The failure is quiet and badly disguised. Audio still plays and the blackout
  screen still works, so nothing looks broken from inside the app — but the
  media session never activates, so there is no notification, no lock-screen
  controls, and on Android the OS is free to kill the playback after a few
  minutes. Debug builds are fine, because nothing is shrunk there.

  Same class of bug as the Room rule in proguard-rules.pro: a dependency the
  tooling cannot see because it is spelled as text.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/audio_service_*" />
